  "ars could be paid out.\"],\n      [\"2017-05\", \"high\", \"May 2017 – January 2018\", \"Swings from $0.92 to $1.21. During the crypto boom USDT was small and illiquid, so the price jumped in both directions. <em>(estimate)</em>\"],\n      [\"2018-10\", \"low\", \"15 Oct 2018\", \"Dropped to $0.93. Doubts about Tether's reserves and Bitfinex's problems with its bank (Noble Bank) triggered a wave of USDT selling.\"],\n      [\"2020-03\", \"range\", \"12–13 Mar 2020\", \"Range $0.90 to $1.08. “Black Thursday”: the crypto market fell about 50% in two days and liquidity vanished on every exchange.\"],\n      [\"2020-08\", \"low\", \"31 Aug 2020\", \"Dropped to $0.89 on the same day as USDC and DAI, with no known event. Probably a data error. <em>(estimate)</em>\"],\n      [\"2022-05\", \"low\", \"12 May 2022\", \"Dropped to $0.95. The collapse of Terra's UST spread panic to all stablecoins, and investors redeemed billions of dollars of USDT within a few days. Tether paid out every redemption and the price recovered.\"],\n      [\"2022-11\", \"low\", \"10 Nov 2022\", \"Dropped to $0.98 during the collapse of the FTX exchange.\"]\n    ],\n    USDC: [\n      [\"2018-11\", \"high\", \"November 2018 – 2020\", \"Range of about $0.97 to $1.06. In its first years USDC had little liquidity on exchanges. <em>(estimate)</em>\"],\n      [\"2020-03\", \"range\", \"12–13 Mar 2020\", \"Range $0.93 to $1.08 during “Black Thursday”.\"],\n      [\"2020-08\", \"low\", \"31 Aug 2020\", \"Dropped to $0.89 on the same day as USDT and DAI. Probably a data error. <em>(estimate)</em>\"]",
